# CK3 script and localization files are byte-sensitive.
#
# Paradox tools expect UTF-8 **with BOM** on localization files, and the engine
# is happy with either line ending as long as it is not rewritten mid-file.
# `-text` on everything tells Git to store the exact bytes it was given and to
# never normalise line endings or encoding. Do not change this lightly: the
# fastest way to break every localization key in the repository is to let Git
# convert these files.
* -text

# Explicit binary types (belt and braces, in case -text is ever relaxed)
*.dds  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.tga  binary
*.bin  binary
*.dmp  binary
*.ck3  binary

# Localization: never merge these automatically; a bad merge silently drops keys
*.yml  -text -merge diff

# Diff these as text so pull requests are readable
*.txt  diff
*.md   diff
*.gui  diff
*.py   diff
*.json diff
